      "writtenOn": "2016-10-06T19:18:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In struct SignedHeader, yes. But the struct returned by the first reply isn\u0027t that, it\u0027s struct first_response_pdu (in upgrade_fw.h), which contains an array of struct signed_header_version. If I add keyid to that, then the updater needs to know both v4 and v5 formats by different names. If I add an array of keyid to the end, then I can use the same struct here, and just ignore the v5 part that\u0027s not included in the v4 response.",
      "parentUuid": "7fd2c819_c496904d",
      "revId": "f995ba48f8f61ef7b6dc97bd69966288143cce7c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd2c819_07079a7a",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/usb_updater.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 690,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-06T19:22:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sure, what I meant to ask was is the separate data oblect target_keyid required? Can the values received from the target be saved in the appropriate fields of target_shv instead?\n\ndoes this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "7fd2c819_27157eae",
      "revId": "f995ba48f8f61ef7b6dc97bd69966288143cce7c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd2c819_07c95aa5",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/usb_updater.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 690,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-06T19:58:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the question I answered. \n\nOn the wire, with v4, struct first_response_pdu looks like this:\n\n  {\n        uint32_t return_value;\n        uint32_t protocol_version;\n        uint32_t  backup_ro_offset;\n        uint32_t  backup_rw_offset;\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n        }\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n        }\n  }\n\nAdding keyid to struct signed_header_version would change it to this:\n\n  {\n        uint32_t return_value;\n        uint32_t protocol_version;\n        uint32_t  backup_ro_offset;\n        uint32_t  backup_rw_offset;\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n          uint32_t keyid;             NEW\n        }\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n          uint32_t keyid;             NEW\n        }\n  }\n\nIf we do this instead:\n\n  {\n        uint32_t return_value;\n        uint32_t protocol_version;\n        uint32_t  backup_ro_offset;\n        uint32_t  backup_rw_offset;\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n        }\n        {\n          uint32_t minor;\n          uint32_t major;\n          uint32_t epoch;\n        }\n  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ same as V4\n        uint32_t keyid[0];            NEW\n        uint32_t keyid[1];            NEW\n  }\n\nThen usb_updater.c doesn\u0027t have to keep track of both the v4 and v5 version\nof struct first_response_pdu. V4 is a strict subset of V5.",
      "parentUuid": "7fd2c819_07079a7a",
      "revId": "f995ba48f8f61ef7b6dc97bd69966288143cce7c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd2c819_2a71c335",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/usb_updater.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 690,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-06T20:14:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah, of course, I and did not look at the code and confused between SignedHeader and signed_header_version structures.\n\n\nBut still I think it would be cleaner to keep a single object for all that data we retrieve from the target in the first protocol reply.\n\nMaybe it is worth storing a first_response_pdu object instead of target_shv and target_keyid, just convert values in it to the machine representation.\n\nThis way when new fields are added to for a new protocol version the object to store them will be already there, just more fields would need to be converted.",
      "parentUuid": "7fd2c819_07c95aa5",
      "revId": "f995ba48f8f61ef7b6dc97bd69966288143cce7c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd2c819_2aeaa39d",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/usb_updater.c",
